  #1 Constructor: NewMotorWriter(pool *pgxpool.Pool) router.Writer; nil pool panics.
  #2 Composition: newSnapshotWriter(pool, "motor_snapshots", motorColumnFor); ctor error panics.
  #3 Map source-of-truth: static motorColumnByField (36 entries) NOT runtime YAML re-read.
  #4 Reflective coverage: TestMotorWriter_ColumnMapMatchesRoutingYAML walks router.LoadMap()
      and asserts (len==36) + (no missing) + (no extra) + (column matches) for DestMotorSnapshot.
  #5 Tests: type matrix (float64 + text only — schema has 33xDOUBLE PRECISION + 5xTEXT,
      no BOOLEAN/INTEGER columns, so bool/int64 cases would not represent any routed field)
      + unknown-field negative (VehicleSpeed; routes to drive_telemetry, guards against widening)
      + nil-pool panic.

Reasoning notes:
  - Schema has power_w column (line 128) that is NOT routed — comment in motor_writer.go
    documents intentional omission: there is no DiPower atomic; per-axle DiTorqueActual* +
    DiAxleSpeed* are the SI inputs from which power is derived downstream.
  - Hvil routes to TEXT column hvil_state; codec emits the protomodel HvilStatus enum as a
    string (per routing.yaml comment lines 482-483) so it slots into bindSnapshotValue's
    string case.
  - DiState{F,R,REL,RER} also TEXT — same string path.
  - Per-corner suffix convention F/R/REL/RER preserved in column names.
  - VIN-resolution contract inherited from snapshot_base (prompt 0010): codec.Atomic.VehicleID
    is the VIN string, not numeric vehicles.id; the snapshot helper's INSERT...SELECT FROM
    vehicles WHERE v.vin =  handles the lookup. No additional handling here.

